# This ref is only ever consumed as `uses: jclaveau/ci-prebuilds/.github/actions/prepare@v0`,
# which makes the runner download the whole repo tarball once a job. Everything the action does
# not need is kept out of that archive: 1,318,679 B -> 3,200 B, clones and actions/checkout
# unaffected (they speak git, not the archive).
#
# Every ancestor directory needs its own un-ignore line: `*` ignores the `.github` directory
# itself, and git then never looks inside it, which yields an EMPTY archive. `!pattern` is not
# negation here either — git warns `Negative patterns are ignored in git attributes`.
* export-ignore
/.github -export-ignore
/.github/actions -export-ignore
/.github/actions/prepare -export-ignore
/.github/actions/prepare/** -export-ignore
